{"ts":"2026-08-08T07:58:25.041Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"79fe526b1f45937aac208eb8","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"1","source":"environment"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.226","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-08-08T07:58:25.041Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"ENOSPC escaped as a raw Node error from the fs.cp calls in the snapshot restore stage, so it was captured as an unactionable production exception naming only a scrubbed copyfile frame. Added withSnapshotFilesystemGuard, a bounded boundary around the create_object and restore_stage filesystem stages that converts host environment faults (ENOSPC/EDQUOT -> workspace_snapshot_storage_exhausted, EACCES/EPERM/EROFS -> workspace_snapshot_permission_denied) into declared PmCliError refusals with recovery guidance. Because shouldCaptureCliError already excludes PmCliError, these host conditions no longer create high Sentry issues at all, which is the correct disposition: a full disk on an operator machine is not a pm defect and must not gate pm releases. The operation label is a fixed identifier and never a path; a test asserts the workspace topology appears in neither the message nor the context. Non-errno failures still propagate untouched so real defects are still reported."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-08T07:58:25.041Z"}],"before_hash":"61a86a5069691cabf5132f185b5325cbe16b50ea136252235b9c4de96cf3b74e","after_hash":"b4bba441545669258d3a3decabb8149628485bf23ea6def2c210d6e0b26257cb"}
{"ts":"2026-08-08T07:59:06.792Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"79fe526b1f45937aac208eb8","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"1","source":"environment"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.226","source":"probe"}},"op":"close","patch":[{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/assignee"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-08T07:59:06.792Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"closed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/closed_at","value":"2026-08-08T07:59:06.742Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/completed_at","value":"2026-08-08T07:59:06.742Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/resolution","value":"withSnapshotFilesystemGuard converts host ENOSPC/EDQUOT/EACCES/EPERM/EROFS faults raised by the create_object and restore_stage stages into declared PmCliError refusals with recovery guidance."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Resource exhaustion reports the bounded operation and recovery path without disclosing workspace topology, and stops creating unactionable high Sentry issues."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Both stages refuse with workspace_snapshot_storage_exhausted or workspace_snapshot_permission_denied; tests assert paths appear in neither message nor context, and non-errno faults still propagate as defects."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Typed environment-fault boundary added around snapshot filesystem stages with path-free actionable guidance; Sentry PM-CLI-2S resolved in next release and the reliability gate now passes."}],"before_hash":"b4bba441545669258d3a3decabb8149628485bf23ea6def2c210d6e0b26257cb","after_hash":"d0b0e8183503eaa6da59f6ff77d66b6484ac3add56c5a66c0f74df17dcfc0c33"}
